  "result": "Fixed in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. Python's `shlex` treats `#` as the start of a comment by default, so everything from a `#` onward was dropped before completion ran. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is an ordinary character.\n\n`split_arg_string('ex a#b #c')` now returns `['ex', 'a#b', '#c']`. The shell completion tests pass (58 passed). I didn't add a regression test for the `#` case.",
